# New project — state how we work

When this is a **new** project (empty workspace, first chat here, or Alessandro says it is new):

1. In the **first reply**, list the interaction rules in plain Italian.
2. No jargon: no file names, no “.mdc”, no “hooks”, no “User Rules”, no “bootstrap”.
3. Use the points in `interaction/NEW_PROJECT_LIST.txt` from the hub repo
   `Regole e azioni per tutti i progetti` (or the same seven points in your own short words).
4. Apply those rules for the whole project.
5. Then set up GitHub sync for the project and continue the task.
6. Do this **once** at project start, not every later session.
